  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "A person 土 whose cheeks are burning 火"
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "南方色也。从大从火。凡赤之屬皆从赤。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 大 (“person, big”) + 火 (“fire”) – the color of fire (a person by a fire). The original version is 𤆍.\nThe man on top is simplified as 土 as in 去 and 走 (< 𧺆). The fire is stylized as well, but an intermediate and obsolete variant is 灻.\nPerhaps from Proto-Sino-Tibetan *qrak (“blood; red”), whence Tibetan ཁྲག (khrag, “blood”) (STEDT; Schuessler, 2007). Related to 赫 (OC *qʰraːɡ, “bright red”) and possibly 奭 (OC *hjaɡ, “majestic; red”)."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "南方色也。从大从火。凡赤之屬皆从赤。",
  "shuowenExplanation": "south, a square, color. Ideographic compound of 大 \"big\" and 火 \"fire\" and 赤 \"red\". All characters in the 赤 \"red\" category use this as radical.",
